Implement Phase 1 of the Payment Module for an enterprise accounting system.

Tech Stack

- Java 21
- Spring Boot
- Spring Data JPA
- Hibernate
- Jakarta Validation
- PostgreSQL

Project Architecture

The project is organized by layer, NOT by feature.

Folders already exist:

entity/
repository/
enums/

Use the project's existing BaseEntity for all entities.

=========================================
OBJECTIVE
=========================================

Create the persistence layer only.

DO NOT create:

- Services
- Controllers
- DTOs
- Mappers
- Validators

Only implement:

- Entities
- Enums
- Repositories

=========================================
PAYMENT ENTITY
=========================================

Create PaymentEntity.

Fields

id (inherit from BaseEntity)

receiptNumber (unique)

customer (ManyToOne CustomerEntity)

paymentDate

receiptDate

paymentMethod (Enum)

bankAccount (ManyToOne ChartOfAccountEntity)

currency

exchangeRate

amountReceived

allocatedAmount

unallocatedAmount

referenceNumber

memo

status (Enum)

attachments

Store attachment IDs as a List<Long> (matching the existing File Upload module used by invoices).

Relationships

One payment belongs to one customer.

One payment has many allocations.

One payment may have many refunds.

=========================================
PAYMENT ALLOCATION ENTITY
=========================================

Create PaymentAllocationEntity.

Fields

id

payment (ManyToOne PaymentEntity)

invoice (ManyToOne InvoiceEntity)

allocatedAmount

notes

Each allocation links exactly one payment to one invoice.

=========================================
PAYMENT REFUND ENTITY
=========================================

Fields

id

payment

refundDate

amount

reason

journalEntry (ManyToOne JournalEntity)

referenceNumber

memo

status

